config.py
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pkl
*.log
.env

# The trained classifier is an exception to *.pkl above. It has to be in the
# repo: scanner.py's score_findings() falls back to p_real=1.0 for every
# finding when the artifact is missing, which silently inflates every risk
# score instead of erroring. Tracking it means a fresh clone (or a Docker
# build) scores identically to this machine, and the evaluation figures in
# NOTES.md are reproducible by someone else. 3.2MB.
!model/risk_classifier.pkl

# timestamped safety copies from `build_eval_sample.py --force`
*.bak

# GuardDog's own virtualenv. It can't live in venv/ or requirements.txt:
# guarddog requires click >=8.4.1 and semgrep pins click ~=8.1.8, so sharing
# an environment silently upgrades click out from under semgrep. Created with
#   python3 -m venv .venv-guarddog && .venv-guarddog/bin/pip install guarddog
.venv-guarddog/

# Local Claude Code tooling, committed by accident in 01fadc6. 70k lines of
# vendored third-party skill code against ~7.7k of MalDet's own, which buried
# the actual diff in every pull request. Config, not project source.
.claude/
.impeccable/

# Built extension bundles — regenerate with extension/build.sh
extension/dist/

# Screenshots and exported bundles for the report/deck — not app source.
# Root-anchored so static/downloads/*.zip (served by the site) stays tracked.
/Product Shots/
/*.zip

# Design references and one-off outputs, kept locally but not published
/image_reference_UI/
/design/dashboard-concept.html
/design/font-options.html
/rescan_requires_login.txt
/rescan_stale_july.txt
